ushes up against the divine, when a seemingly ordinary person discovers that fate has been watching them all along. With the rules of Origins-to-Hero advancement woven naturally into the narrative, this introduction serves as the first spark in a saga where myth rises beneath the desert sun. About the Chronicle The Valley of the Setting Sun is a Scion Second Edition chronicle set in modern-day Phoenix, where divine power sleeps just beneath the heat-hazed pavement. The campaign follows a band of Scions as they awaken to their true heritage, receive their Visitations, and step into a world woven with prophecy, danger, and the weight of mythic legacy. Each prelude explores a different character&rsquo;s emergence into the divine&mdash;and sets up the heroic path ahead as they confront Titanspawn, hidden threats, and the shifting balance between fate and free will. \ud83d\udde8\ufe0f Hop into our Discord! Love the stories? Want to chat with the storyteller and players? Or maybe you're just looking for a place to geek out about tabletop roleplaying games? Whether you're a seasoned GM, a curious newbie, or just love hearing epic tales unfold, our community is the perfect place to hang out, ask questions, share your own adventures, and connect with fellow TTRPG fans. Come say hi&mdash;we&rsquo;d love to meet you! \ud83d\udc49 https://discord.gg/T9zeN9p Follow Us X: https://x.com/Twin_Cities_VtM Facebook: https://www.facebook.com/TwinCitiesByNight/ iTunes: https://itunes.apple.com/us/podcast/twin-cities-by-night/id1246523585?mt=2 SoundCloud: https://soundcloud.com/twin-cities-by-night YouTube: https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCBUyj7h-xIhwsM3kHK56SRA &nbsp; &nbsp; </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Join us in the character creation, as the characters from 'A Light Extinguished' and 'The Siege of Shadow Valley Ranch' are visited by their divine parents and become Heroes.<br /> <br /> 'Valley of the Setting Sun' is a Scion Second Edition game. Scion Second Edition is owned and 